WEBVTT

00:00:04.765 --> 00:00:07.520
To fully harness the potential of Microsoft 365

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.048
Copilot, users should adopt best practices that ensure

00:00:12.048 --> 00:00:17.280
effective, secure, and ethical interactions with the AI.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.056
The quality of Copilot’s output depends heavily on the

00:00:21.056 --> 00:00:25.850
clarity and structure of your prompts. So Be Specific:

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.234
The more detailed your prompt, the better

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.030
Copilot can meet your needs.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.090
For example, instead of saying, “Explain this

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.178
document,” a more effective prompt would be,

00:00:37.178 --> 00:00:40.706
“Summarize this technical document in three bullet

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:43.830
points suitable for a non-technical audience.”

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.630
Iterate and Refine:

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.130
Copilot thrives on user feedback.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:53.412
If the response isn’t quite right, rephrase

00:00:53.412 --> 00:00:55.780
or add more details to your prompt.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.844
For instance, if you’re unsatisfied with a report

00:00:58.844 --> 00:01:02.044
draft, you can guide Copilot with commands like,

00:01:02.044 --> 00:01:06.068
“Rewrite this section to emphasize cost efficiency.”

00:01:06.068 --> 00:01:11.316
Experiment with Creativity: Beyond structured tasks,

00:01:11.316 --> 00:01:13.340
Copilot is a powerful tool for

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.276
brainstorming and generating innovative ideas.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.348
Ask it for alternative headlines, creative slide

00:01:19.348 --> 00:01:22.300
titles, or new ways to present data.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.124
As with any AI tool,

00:01:24.124 --> 00:01:27.188
maintaining data privacy is paramount.

00:01:27.188 --> 00:01:30.580
Use Copilot within trusted, organization-approved platforms

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.220
to ensure compliance with data security protocols.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.852
Avoid sharing unnecessary personal or sensitive information

00:01:37.852 --> 00:01:40.540
and ensure that any shared data is

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:43.280
encrypted and anonymized when possible.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:48.130
For example, instead of uploading raw customer details,

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:52.050
work with summarized or generalized datasets.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.326
Familiarize yourself with how Copilot accesses

00:01:55.326 --> 00:01:58.894
your organization's data (emails, documents, etc.),

00:01:58.894 --> 00:01:59.942
ensuring it’s in line with

00:01:59.942 --> 00:02:02.078
your company’s privacy policies.

00:02:02.078 --> 00:02:06.014
And most importantly, always review and verify

00:02:06.014 --> 00:02:08.645
AI outputs to ensure they align with

00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:11.070
your intentions and ethical standards.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.962
AI models can inadvertently reflect

00:02:13.962 --> 00:02:16.050
biases in their training data.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.754
Be vigilant in identifying and correcting any biases

00:02:19.754 --> 00:02:23.714
in Copilot’s responses, especially when generating content or

00:02:23.714 --> 00:02:26.470
making decisions that could impact others.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.466
And when presenting Copilot-generated outputs to

00:02:30.466 --> 00:02:33.030
stakeholders, be clear about its role.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.422
Transparency builds trust and sets realistic

00:02:37.422 --> 00:02:41.170
expectations about AI’s capabilities and limitations.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.334
By following these practices, users

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.854
can maximize Copilot’s potential while

00:02:46.854 --> 00:02:50.242
upholding privacy, security, and responsibility.